The ISR thread in `tegra_qspi_isr_thread` checks `tqspi->curr_xfer` without holding the spinlock, opening a race window where the timeout path (CPU1) can set `curr_xfer` to NULL between the check and the later locked access. When the handlers then dereference `t` (e.g., `t->len`), it causes a NULL pointer dereference.

