 	if (!tqspi->curr_xfer) {
+		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&tqspi->lock, flags);
 		...
 	}
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&tqspi->lock, flags);

// in handle_cpu_based_xfer and handle_dma_based_xfer:
 	t = tqspi->curr_xfer;
+	if (!t) {
+		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&tqspi->lock, flags);
+		return IRQ_HANDLED;
+	}
```
Reason:
The initial NULL check in `tegra_qspi_isr_thread` is now protected by the spinlock, preventing the race between the ISR and timeout path. Additionally, the handlers now re-check `tqspi->curr_xfer` under the lock after acquisition and safely return if it has been cleared, ensuring that even if the timeout path set it to NULL after the ISR thread acquired the lock but before the handler runs, the dereference is avoided.

